> 1. **Full Path to Rscript:** Modify your Julia script (`combo.jl`) to use the full path to `Rscript`. In your `combo.jl`, change:
>    ```julia
>    run(`Rscript eval.R`)
>    ```
>    to:
>    ```julia
>    run(`/usr/local/bin/Rscript eval.R`)
>    ```
>    This ensures that the correct `Rscript` is being called regardless of the environment `PATH`.
> 
> 2. **Verify Permissions:** Make sure the script `eval.R` and the directories it is in are readable and executable by the user running the cron job.
> 
> 3. **Cron Jobs and Paths:** If the issue were related to a cron job instead of `launchd`, you could add `PATH` definitions at the top of your cron file. Since macOS uses `launchd`, you'll need to check your `.plist` file instead.
